e again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Perfect negatives do not add did; not follows the existing auxiliary.","B":"The -ing form needs been for a perfect continuous, which is not requested.","C":"In the standard finite negative, not follows the auxiliary.","D":"Place **not after have** and keep **held**: they have not held."}}},{"id":"c6516f4a-913e-5912-a02f-97c4c0c448d6","topicSlug":"present-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Begin this present-perfect question: ____ they held the door open up to now?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Has"},{"id":"B","text":"Have"},{"id":"C","text":"Did"},{"id":"D","text":"Are"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The first auxiliary moves before the subject; do not add a new auxiliary.","explanation":"Move **have** before they. The participle held remains after the subject.","keywords":["perfect-question"],"skill":"perfect-question","contextKey":"present-perfect-48","fingerprint":"4a2c5d542ab5ebc61031eaf309a46ee0d36ec24b1f9ef1b561dd0c74ee2df617","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-present-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The first auxiliary moves before the subject; do not add a new auxiliary.","Move **have** before they. The participle held remains after the subject.","Choose **Have**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Has does not agree with they, and cannot form a past-perfect question.","B":"Move **have** before they. The participle held remains after the subject.","C":"Did would require a base verb and would not make this perfect question.","D":"Are would create a different structure, not the requested perfect."}}},{"id":"3f15428a-6923-5542-ab09-26d49772ff39","topicSlug":"present-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Choose the participle for the present perfect: We have ____ the door open up to now. (